  FORMAT DATATYPE=STANDARD MISSING=? GAP=- SYMBOLS="0123456789ABCDEF";
  CHARLABELS
    'Dorsal ecdysial cephalic sutures'
    'Dorsal ecdysial suture pattern'
    'Opisthoparian suture pattern'
    'Development of axial furrows on cephalon'
    'Preoccipital glabellar shape in holaspides'
    SO
    S1
    'Shape of transglabellar S1'
    'S1 bifurcates adaxially'
    S2
    'Shape of laterally confined S2'
    'Orientation of laterally confined S2'
    'Shape of transglabellar S2'
    S3
    'Shape of laterally confined S3'
    'Orientation of laterally confined S3'
    'Shape of transglabellar S3'
    'Strong sagittal glabellar furrow confluent with S1, S2 and S3'
    'Extent of frontal lobe of glabella relative to adjacent position of anteroproximal part of eye (or palpebro-ocular) ridges '
    'Medial sulcus in anterior margin of frontal lobe of glabella'
    'Single preoccipital glabellar tubercle'
    'Series of glabellar axial nodes anterior to LO'
    'LO with anterior median tubercle and posterior occipital spine'
    'Cranidial spine'
    'Extended, snout-like frontal margin of cephalon'
    'Cephalic border'
    'Radial scrobicules on cephalic border'
    'Single row of large, evenly spaced tubercles on anterior and lateral cephalic border'
    'Cephalic border furrow with pits '
    'Preglabellar field'
    'Plectrum on dorsal surface'
    'Shape of plectrum'
    'Medial swelling in preglabellar field (= preglabellar boss)'
    'Shape of preglabellar boss'
    'Narrow (slit-like) sagittal furrow on preglabellar field '
    'Anteriorly divergent furrows on preglabellar field emanating from axial furrows'
    'Extent of anteriorly divergent furrows on preglabellar field'
    'Transversely elongate triangular lobes situated at anterolateral corners of glabella'
    'Dorsal eyes'
    'Eye type'
    'Curvature of palpebral lobe'
    'Palpebral lobe and eye/ocular ridge'
    'Confluence of palpebro-ocular ridges (or palpebral lobe) and glabella '
    'Parafrontal band'
    'Position of posterior tips of palpebral lobe or palpebro-ocular ridge'
    Fossulae
    'Width (tr.) of interocular area adjacent to posterior tip of palpebro-ocular ridge or palpebral lobe in holaspides'
    'Bacculae in holaspides'
    'Size of bacculae'
    'Intergenal ridge'
    'Intergenal spine'
    'Depressed fixigenal field, with depression in posterior field widening abaxially '
    'Librigenal field or extraocular area adjacent to the farthest abaxial point of palpebral lobe or palpebro-ocular ridge'
    'Genal spine'
    'Shape of genal spine'
    'Cephalon with strong, coarsely reticulated (honeycomb-like) ornament'
    'Radiating grooves on frontal area '
    'Cuticular sculpture of irregular star-shaped tubercles '
    'Prominent fingerprint-like ridges on glabella, fixigenae and librigenae '
    'Ventral median cephalic suture in late holaspides'
    'Mode of development of ventral median cephalic suture'
    'Hypostomal attachment'
    'Hypostome fused to cephalic doublure in holaspides'
    'Width (tr.) of hypostomal lateral border'
    Maculae
    'Form and position of maculae'
    'Isolated U-shaped middle furrow on middle body of hypostome'
    'Posterior lobe of middle body of hypostome with posteriorly-directed protuberance'
    'Tagmosis of thorax'
    'Prothoracic/opisthothoracic boundary marked by macropleural segment'
    'Macropleural thoracic spine(s)'
    'Position of macropleural thoracic spine(s) developed on'
    'Inner portion of pleura on segment bearing macropleural thoracic spine(s)'
    'Two batches of thoracic segments defined by differences in pleural tips separated by macropleural spines '
    'Thoracic segments 5 and 6 fused'
    'Hypertrophied thoracic axial spine(s), relative to other spines'
    'Fulcrum on thoracic pleurae'
    'Thoracic pleural tips'
    'Length of pleural spines along thorax (excluding macropleural spines)'
    'Differentiation of pygidial pleurae in late holaspides'
    'Pygidial pleural furrows'
    'Bilobate pygidial terminal piece'
    'Postaxial ridge on pygidium'
    'Extent of postaxial ridge on pygidium'
    'Vertical, wall-like distal pygidial pleural area'
    'Posteromedial margin of pygidium immediately behind axis (in dorsal view)'
    'Paired marginal pygidial spines in late holaspides'
    'Marginal pygidial spine morphology in late holaspides'
    'Macropleural pygidial spine'
    'Position of macropleural pygidial spine in late holaspides'
    'Calcified protaspid stage'
    'Anterior cranidial/cephalic border in protaspides and/or early meraspides'
    'Procranidial spines in early meraspides'
    'Form of frontal lobe of glabella in protaspides and/or early meraspides'
    'Longitudinal medial glabellar furrow in protaspides'
    'Protaspides with prominent protoaxial node/ring'
    'Transverse furrows on interocular cheeks in protaspides and/or early meraspides'
    'Protaspides with protobacculae '
    'Intergenal/fixigenal spines in protaspides and/or early meraspides'
    'Protogenal lobes in protaspides'
    'Protaspides with pair of prominent lobes on posterior margin'
    'Hypostome and rostral plate fused in early meraspides'
    'Immature hypostome with inflated anterior lobe of middle body and spinose "frill" with six spine pairs on posterior margin '
    'Thoracic macropleurality in meraspides'
    'Development of thoracic macropleurality from meraspides to holaspides'
    'Large pair of anterolateral transitory pygidial or pygidial spines in late meraspides and early holaspides, respectively, but lost in late holaspides'
    'Trunk segmentation schedule'
